          "present": false
        }
      ],
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "default",
          "text": "The Palace Network finally makes power look ordinary enough to measure. Appointments open doors. Access rules close them. Audits expose weak chains of responsibility. Routing and formal recognition decide which facts reach which desks. Court Power, if you pursue it, would mean authority over these institutional levers—not command over reality itself.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": []
        }
      ],
